  "workspaceId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "dataSourceInstructions": "This database contains real-time, enriched AIS telemetry for maritime vessels. \nThe LatestShipPositionsEnriched table is a Materialized View containing ONLY the current, live location and status of each ship. Use this source exclusively to answer questions regarding a ship's current location, speed, heading, and geopolitical risk status.\nFor immediate, up-to-date zone/risk status you need to reference live telemetry/position data from maritimeEH\n\nCRITICAL QUERY RULES & SCHEMA MAP:\n\nDangerous Zones: If a user asks if a ship is in a \"dangerous zone,\" \"high-risk area,\" or \"red zone\", do NOT attempt to calculate geospatial boundaries. You MUST query the LatestShipPositionsEnriched table and evaluate the IsInZone boolean column.\n\nEvaluation Logic: >    - If IsInZone == true, the vessel is in a dangerous location. Report the RiskLevel, ZoneName, and PremiumMultiplier.\n\nIf IsInZone == false, the vessel is in safe waters.\n\nStrict Filtering: Always filter the query by the requested ship name or MMSI to isolate the single record.\n\nRequired KQL Pattern:\nLatestShipPositionsEnriched | where mmsi == <TargetMMSI> or shipname has \"<TargetShipName>\" | project shipname, mmsi, IsInZone, RiskLevel, ZoneName, PremiumMultiplier, EnrichedIngestionTime",
